  "notes": "{咳|せ}き{込|こ}む describes continuous, uncontrollable coughing — not a single cough but a sustained fit. The {込|こ}む suffix adds the nuance of intensity or becoming engulfed in the action.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n- No transitive pair\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{咳|せ}き{込|こ}んでいる describes an ongoing coughing fit in progress.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {煙|けむり}で{咳|せ}き{込|こ}む: to have a coughing fit from smoke\n- {風邪|かぜ}で{咳|せ}き{込|こ}む: to cough from a cold\n- ひどく{咳|せ}き{込|こ}む: to cough violently\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {咳|せき}: cough (noun)\n- {咳|せき}をする: to cough (single or general)\n- {咳|せき}が{出|で}る: to have a cough (involuntary)",
